    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n85246" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύπους</span></b>  (A), ὁ, ἡ, neut. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πουν;</span>
		acc. masc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύποδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pol.</u>
					1281b6
				</span></i>
			: neut. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολύποδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Epin.</u>
					981d
				</span></i>
			:—<i>many-footed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				92a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.35
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐρινύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					488
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὕτω τι πολύπουν ἐστὶν ἡ λύπη κακόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Posidipp.
					19
				</span></i>
			 (dub.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>trodden by many feet,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῶρος</span> Orac. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				6.53
			</span></i>.</div>
